--TEST--
Only an attribute declaration may follow `#[` or be a retrieval's type argument, so a class, a `type` alias, an enum or an inline shape there does not compile — `rule:attributes/an-attribute-is-declared-with-its-sites`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: lang:attributes/an-attribute-is-declared-with-the-places-it-may-be-used
namespace Shop;

attribute Job on method { queue: string }

class Mailer {}
type Address = { street: string };
enum Size { Small = 1, Large = 2 }

// `Job` is an attribute declaration, so its use and its retrieval compile.
class Accepted {
    #[Job(queue: "mail")]
    public function send(): int {
        return 1;
    }
}
var $job = Core\Attributes::get<Job>(Accepted::send);

// Each name below is not an attribute declaration.
#[Mailer(queue: "mail")]
class WithAClass {}

#[Address(street: "Main Street 1")]
class WithAnAlias {}

#[Size]
class WithAnEnum {}

var $shape = Core\Attributes::get<{name: string}>(Accepted::send);

echo "unreachable\n";
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E1005]: only an attribute declaration may follow `#[`, and `Mailer` is a class
   --> case.nvs:21:3
%A
error[E1005]: only an attribute declaration may follow `#[`, and `Address` is a `type` alias
   --> case.nvs:24:3
%A
error[E1005]: only an attribute declaration may follow `#[`, and `Size` is an enum
   --> case.nvs:27:3
%A
error[E1008]: a retrieval's type argument must name an attribute declaration, and `{ name: string }` is a shape type
   --> case.nvs:30:35
%A
error: aborting due to 4 errors
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
